      "writtenOn": "2020-04-03T17:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think OptionalPath should only be used if the input (symbol_file property in this case) is allowed to be null or non-null. However, in this case it is not. What flagged this usage up for me was that you never call the OptionalPath.Valid() method.\n\nGenerally using OptionalPath for what is essentially a required Path prevents failing fast which can make things more difficult to debug. Obviously, in this case that is not true because if symbol_file is not set then the call to compileStubLibrary() will fail. However, it seems a little fragile to rely on that.\n\nIf you used Path then in the non-stubs case you would just end up with a nil Path.\n\nI didn\u0027t realize that compileStubLibrary was used in quite so many places.",
      "parentUuid": "e8d0d995_908dd021",
      "revId": "c5dd4f7c1f3958bb68ad493088275b286a6acd6b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
